1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,450
That voice on the recording really is you.

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:05,110
When you talk, you hear yourself two ways.

3
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:08,960
Sound leaves your mouth and travels through the air into your ears,

4
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:11,170
the same way everyone else hears it.

5
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:14,360
But it also travels straight through the bones of your skull,

6
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:17,730
and that path makes your voice sound deeper and fuller.

7
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:20,760
A recording only catches the sound in the air,

8
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:24,070
so it sounds thinner and higher than the voice in your head.

9
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:25,190
The good news?

10
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:29,500
In one study, people rated their own recorded voice as more attractive,

11
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:31,710
as long as they didn't recognize it.

12
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:34,010
So next time you hear yourself on a video,

13
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,067
don't cringe, because
